    "done_when": "With the plan subsection definitions-2026-09-29 with its addendum and its gpu-watch scope item governs wherever the section text leaves room: watch.py reads the estimate record through one function from the price table's directory joined with third-party-cache-rate.json, and prices each period as h x input x cache-read rate + (1 - h) x input x prompt rate + output x completion rate at the rate in force (price_at), printing exactly one cost figure per period row with a label giving h as a percentage, the source kind and the citation, and carrying the same figure and label in the --json period rows; tests in tests/test_agent_watch_cost.py over a fixture period with non-zero input, cached and output tokens, a fixture price row and a fixture record pin the figure by literal, assert neither the own-cache figure (ledger_cost) nor the h=0 figure appears in the output, and assert the label; the worker writes no file outside the repository, and a missing record renders a dash with the label stating that no estimate is installed, asserted by a test (installing the measured record is the coordinator's deploy step); gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_agent_watch_cost.py tests/test_agent_telemetry_watch.py tests/test_agent_watch_live.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status",
